\title{Biconditional}
\date{2026-01-28T21:12:12Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Let #{P} and #{Q} be propositions.  The \em{biconditional} #{P \iff Q} (pronounced "#{P} if and only if #{Q}") is true when #{P} and #{Q} have the same truth value, and false otherwise.}
